<title>UK: Air Canada to fly aero-engine to Boeing.</title>
<headline>Air Canada to fly aero-engine to Boeing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air Canada expects to fly a Rolls Royce jet engine from London to Vancouver on Friday, its UK cargo manager Mike Judkins said.</p>
<p>Rolls aviation engines are then trucked to Boeing in Seattle, he said, adding that each year Air Canada take some 20 to 30 engines to Seattle.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
